WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.982
An arcade pays out prizes in tokens of the values listed in tokens, and the machine has an

2
00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:11.046
unlimited supply of each value. Return the fewest tokens needed to pay out exactly amount. If the amount

3
00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:16.105
cannot be formed exactly, return -1. An amount of 0 needs zero tokens.

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.335
Three 5-tokens use fewer tokens than 12 + 1 + 1 + 1, so greedy largest-first is wrong

5
00:00:23.335 --> 00:00:23.714
here.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.899
Every combination of 4 and 6 is even, so 7 is impossible.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.718
Every amount's answer depends only on smaller amounts, so computing amounts in increasing order guarantees each

8
00:00:38.718 --> 00:00:39.950
dependency is ready.

9
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.995
Create a table where fewest[v] is the fewest tokens for amount v. Set fewest[0] = 0 and everything

10
00:00:47.995 --> 00:00:53.099
else to infinity. For each amount from 1 upward and each token that fits, take the better of

11
00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:56.555
the current value and fewest[v - token] + 1.

12
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.530
I build a table from 0 to the amount where each entry is the minimum over tokens of

13
00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:09.676
the entry one token lower plus one. Infinity marks unreachable amounts and turns into -1 at the end.

14
00:01:09.676 --> 00:01:16.621
The table has amount + 1 entries and each considers every token, giving O(amount × tokens) time and

15
00:01:16.621 --> 00:01:20.823
O(amount) space, and unlike a greedy pass it is correct for any token set.

16
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:30.529
For tokens [1, 5, 12] and amount 15, the table reads 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 1, 2,

17
00:01:30.529 --> 00:01:34.504
3, 4, 5, 2 for amounts 0–10.

18
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.576
Amounts 11–14 become 3, 1, 2, 3, and amount 15 takes the minimum of fewest[14] + 1 =

19
00:01:44.576 --> 00:01:50.753
4, fewest[10] + 1 = 3 and fewest[3] + 1 = 4.

20
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.598
So fewest[15] = 3, achieved by three 5-tokens.

21
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.522
O(amount × tokens). O(amount)
